# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# NOTE: every pattern below is anchored to the repository root (leading "/") on purpose.
# Unanchored globs such as "coverage.*", ".env" or "go.work" also match files inside the
# committed vendor/ tree (e.g. vendor/golang.org/x/text/language/coverage.go). Git silently
# drops those files from the commit, which leaves vendor/ incomplete and breaks
# `make build` on a fresh clone.

# Binaries for programs and plugins
/*.exe
/*.exe~
/*.dll
/*.so
/*.dylib

# Test binary, built by `go test -c`
/*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
/*.out
/coverage.*
/*.coverprofile
/profile.cov

# Dependency directories
# vendor/ is intentionally NOT ignored: it is committed so builds are reproducible
# without network access. After changing imports run `make tidy && make vendor`
# and commit the result.

# Go workspace file
/go.work
/go.work.sum

# env file
/.env

# build
/bin
/air

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
